          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">The protein blend</h3>

          <p>
            The protein comes from a 51 g "Smoothie King Pro-Sorb Blend" of whey protein isolate, whey protein hydrolysate, micellar casein and egg white solids. Because it is a proprietary blend, the label does not say how much of each protein is in the scoop. Ingredients are listed in descending order by weight, so whey isolate is the largest, but the split between fast whey and slower casein is unknown. On top of that sits a 3 g PepForm amino peptide blend (leucine, glutamine, isoleucine and valine peptides), which is where the front-label claims of 12 g BCAAs and 7 g glutamine and precursors come from.
          </p>

          <p>
            The published amino acid profile is the strongest part of the label. Per serving, Smoothie King lists 47.4 g of total amino acids, including 5.8 g of leucine, 3.3 g of isoleucine and 3.0 g of valine. Few brands publish this at all. For context, about 2.5 to 3 g of leucine is the amount often cited as enough to trigger muscle protein synthesis in one meal, so a full Gladiator serving clears that easily; a single scoop is closer to the line at roughly 2.9 g.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Sweetener, gums and extras</h3>

          <p>
            The other ingredients on the chocolate label are natural flavors, alkalized cocoa powder, xanthan gum, sunflower oil, vegetable fiber, sucralose and guar gum. Strawberry adds beet powder for color. Sucralose is the only sweetener, and the two gums thicken the shake. There is also a 125 mg "Digest-Pro" enzyme blend of Aminogen, protease, amylase, lipase and lactase, and a vitamin and mineral panel with 50 to 300 percent of the daily value for most vitamins, plus 250 mg of calcium and 9 mg of iron.
          </p>
