        <div id="third-party-tested" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            5. Is Gladiator Protein Third-Party Tested?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Yes. Smoothie King Gladiator Chocolate, Vanilla and Strawberry are each listed in NSF's Certified for Sport registry, and the NSF Certified for Sport mark is printed on the front of the tub. We checked the registry ourselves: the listings show the 907 g tub and the single-serve packet, serving sizes, macros and a run of certified lot numbers. That is the strongest testing claim a protein powder can make in the US, and it is unusual for a restaurant chain's own-label product.
          </p>

          <p>
            NSF Certified for Sport means NSF tests the product for the substances banned by major sports organizations, checks that the label matches what is in the tub, screens for contaminants and audits the manufacturing facility. It is the program named by the NFL, MLB, NHL and many college programs, which is why tested athletes look for it. Our <a href="/best-nsf-certified-protein-powder/">best NSF certified protein powder</a> guide explains the program in more detail and ranks the other certified powders.
          </p>

          <p>
            Two caveats. First, certification applies to specific lots and products, so check the lot number on your tub against the NSF listing if you are drug-tested; the registry shows the lot numbers it covers. Second, NSF Certified for Sport is not a heavy-metals rating. We found no published heavy-metal results for Gladiator from Clean Label Project or similar groups, so we cannot say how it compares on lead or cadmium.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-3">THE CHECK</p>
            <p class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Verify the lot, not just the logo</p>
            <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed m-0">If you are a tested athlete, search "Smoothie King Gladiator" on the NSF Certified for Sport site and compare the lot number printed on your tub with the lots listed. Ask the store for a fresher tub if yours is not covered.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

